{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y_obs`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that the top-level parameters `rho`, `alpha`, and `sigma` are each given their built-in prior before they are used to build the Gaussian-process covariance. The covariance and Cholesky factor computation was inlined into the `multi_normal_cholesky` likelihood. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N_obs;
  array[N_obs] real x_obs;
  vector[N_obs] y_obs;
}

parameters {
  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

model {
  rho ~ inv_gamma(4.6, 22.1); // P[rho < 2.0] \approx 0.01, P[rho > 20] \approx 0.01
  alpha ~ normal(0, 2);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  y_obs ~ multi_normal_cholesky(
    rep_vector(0, N_obs),
    cholesky_decompose(  gp_exp_quad_cov(x_obs, alpha, rho)
                       + diag_matrix(rep_vector(square(sigma), N_obs))));
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N_obs":1,"x_obs":[5.620919443633133],"y_obs":[1.0]}","protected_variables":["y_obs"]}
